{"id":76,"text":"An old dog named Rex lived on a farm. He was slow and grey, and he slept most of the day. Then the farmer brought home a lively puppy named Buddy, who ran around the yard barking at everything.\n\n“Why do you sleep so much?” asked Buddy. “You’re so boring! Come and play with me!”\n\n“I’m tired, young one,” said Rex. “I’ve worked hard for ten years.”\n\nBuddy ignored him and continued running in circles. One day, he found a small hole in the fence and squeezed through it. Soon he was in the forest, excited by the strange smells and sounds.\n\nThen he saw something move in the bushes. It was a fox, and it was looking straight at him. Buddy froze. He wanted to run, but his legs wouldn’t move.\n\nSuddenly, a deep bark shook the air. Rex had followed him. The old dog stepped in front of the puppy and showed his teeth. His voice was low and fierce. The fox hesitated, then turned and disappeared into the trees.\n\nOn the way home, Buddy walked quietly beside the old dog. “I’m sorry,” he said. “I didn’t understand.”\n\n“You were curious,” said Rex. “That’s good. But wisdom comes from experience, not from speed.”\n\nFrom then on, Buddy listened to Rex and learned everything the old dog could teach him.\n\nMoral: Respect the experience of older people, because they have seen what you haven’t.","tr":null,"gl":{"an":"bir (noaniq artikl)","old":"keksa, eski","dog":"it","named":"ismli","rex":"Reks (it nomi)","lived":"yashardi","on":"ustida, -da","a":"bir (noaniq artikl)","farm":"ferma","he":"u (erkak)","was":"edi","slow":"sekin","and":"va","grey":"kulrang","slept":"uxladi","most":"eng","of":"-ning; -dan","the":"(aniq artikl)","day":"kun","then":"keyin, so'ng","farmer":"dehqon","brought":"olib keldi","home":"uy","lively":"jonli","puppy":"kuchukcha","buddy":"do'stim, oshna","who":"kim; -gan (kishi)","ran":"yugurdi","around":"atrofida","yard":"hovli","barking":"hurayotgan","at":"-da, -ga","everything":"hamma narsa","why":"nega","do":"qilmoq","you":"sen, siz","sleep"